__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.env
# A pattern containing a "/" (other than a trailing one) is anchored to
# this file's own directory in git's gitignore semantics -- the entries
# below only ever matched a `.decoy/` at the repo ROOT. Confirmed
# empirically as a real gap: running this project's own tests from
# vscode-extension/ or intellij-plugin/ (both spawn a real decoy
# chat-proxy process, which creates its own local .decoy/ under whatever
# cwd it inherits) left a real vault.key sitting untracked-but-NOT-
# ignored under vscode-extension/.decoy/ -- `git check-ignore` confirmed
# it matched nothing. The leading `**/` below matches `.decoy/` at any
# depth, closing that gap for good instead of anchoring to one location.
**/.decoy/vault.key
**/.decoy/vault.key.lock
**/.decoy/*.local.json
**/.decoy/audit.enc
**/.decoy/audit.enc.lock
**/.decoy/vault.enc
**/.decoy/vault.enc.lock
**/.decoy/audit.log*
node_modules/
dist/
out/
build/
*.class
.gradle/
.idea/
